<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adarnase IV of Iberia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/923">923</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adarnase IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> was a Bagratid prince of Tao-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klarjeti">Klarjeti</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. In 888 he took the title king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberians">Iberians</a>, restoring Georgian kingship after about three centuries, and ruled until 923. He balanced between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and the Bagratid kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, and his descendants went on to unite the Georgian lands into the Kingdom of Georgia around 1008.</p></div>
